## G1 — offline rendering mechanism verified against the installed lib

`MockConnection` = `sqlalchemy.engine.mock.MockConnection` (`alembic/runtime/migration.py:23,36,672`
via `MockEngineStrategy.MockConnection = MockConnection`). It exposes `.execute(obj, params)` whose
impl is Alembic's `dump` → `impl._exec`; with `as_sql=True`, `DefaultImpl._exec`
(`alembic/ddl/impl.py:209-237`) compiles the construct and writes `static_output`. Hence
`op.execute(str)` renders offline. Online path is left on `exec_driver_sql` (byte-identical).

Helper-split diff shape: `fts.py` gains `ddl_statements() -> tuple[str, ...]`; `_ddl` becomes
`for statement in ddl_statements(): connection.exec_driver_sql(statement)`. sg017 `upgrade()` adds an
`if op.get_context().as_sql:` branch that emits each statement through `op.execute` and returns before
the online-only `install_asset_fts(..., rebuild=True)`.

